      "text": "The heart does not purify or clean the blood directly. 🫀 Its main job is to pump blood to organs that perform different functions.\n\nThree important organs are involved:\n\n🫀 Heart: Pumps blood throughout the body.\n\n🫁 Lungs: Remove carbon dioxide from the blood and add oxygen.\n\nKidneys: Filter waste products and excess water from the blood, producing urine.\n\nThe liver also helps process toxins, medications, and waste substances.\n\nHow does it work?\n\nBody → Heart\n\nBlood returns with less oxygen and more carbon dioxide\n\nLungs\n\nCarbon dioxide is removed and oxygen is added\n\nHeart → Body\n\nOxygen-rich blood is pumped throughout the body\n\nMeanwhile, the kidneys continuously filter blood, removing waste and helping maintain the right balance of water and salts.\n\nRemember: The heart is the pump, the lungs are responsible for gas exchange, and the kidneys are the body's main blood filters.\n\nWould you like to learn why blood goes to the lungs before returning to the heart, instead of going directly to the body?",
